<title>UK: Dixons buys DN Computer for 9.7 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Dixons buys DN Computer for 9.7 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dixons Group Plc said on Monday that it has bought DN Computer Services Plc (DNCS) for 9.7 million stg in loan notes and cash.</p>
<p>DNCS is a mail order business, specialising in the supply of computers and computer related products to the business market.  </p>
<p>DNCS employs 130 staff and is based in Heywood, near Manchester. Turnover at the company reached 25 million stg for the year ending 30th April 1996.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
